- op: discuss  # bf21
  at: '2026-07-03T10:23:38Z'  # bf21
  by: agent  # bf21
  actor: jgstern_agent  # bf21
  clock: 3  # bf21
  nonce: bf21  # bf21
  message: "WI-noham Part A shipped in PR #404 (dev 3fbdf0d0d3). py.py now stamps meta['receiver_type_hint'] on unresolved method-call edges when the receiver type is inferred (var_types, or a bare local class name — scope-guarded against a local var/param shadowing a module class per INV-fahub); the inherited_calls linker resolves them via a new strict INV-fahub Site-2 mode (Step-3 type-symbol fallback gated off + same-name-class ambiguity guard for non-legacy langs; _LEGACY_SITE2_LANGS={java}, decoupled from _MRO_WALKERS). Taint-safe (analyzer never flips is_resolved; linker is sole minter). Designed + adversarially reviewed via Workflow; the review caught a shadowed-class false-resolution blocker (fixed + locked). Part A closes ONLY the walker-independent recall: local Class.staticmethod()/classmethod() + typed-receiver-DIRECT (linker Step-1). STAYS OPEN — the flagship @property deadness (Symbol.end_line 260 refs, ValidationResult.ok 47 refs — attribute READS, not calls) is deferred to WI-gubar (D2); the inherited-method mass (needs a Python MRO walker) to WI-hiziz (D1); concrete-class-id precision to WI-supat (D3). Per closure-evidence discipline, do NOT mark satisfied until the flagship repros clear under dead-code-maybe --seeds all (that evidence lives on WI-gubar). Tagged awaits_bakeoff_validation: re-measure the INV-nuzas 283-twin residual + the decorated/plain deadness deltas."  # bf21
