  message: "WI-supat/D3 (the SOLE remaining engineering residual) COMPLETE + CLOSED (done) — PR-A (dev ef2544220c) + PR-B (dev 0ca939118f). So the FULL receiver/self/field-inherited resolution mass is now landed: Part A (typed-receiver-direct + local static/classmethod), D2/WI-gubar (@property reads), D1/WI-hiziz (Site-2 C3 inherited, Site-1 self.method(), Site-3 self.field.method()), D3/WI-supat (concrete-class-id collision precision).\n\nCRITICAL CONTEXT for the bakeoff re-measure: WI-supat's concrete-id path was INERT end-to-end until PR-B's finalize.py fix (_relativize_ir_paths didn't relativize Edge.meta / dict-shaped Symbol.meta, so the ids stayed absolute and missed the relativized class_symbols index -> silent name-path fallback). IMPORTANT: this affected ONLY WI-supat (id-based). The earlier pieces (Part A/B, WI-gubar, WI-hiziz) use NAME hints (receiver_type_hint / enclosing_class / inherited_field_receiver — strings without embedded paths), so they were NEVER affected and fire correctly. So the deadness-delta from the name-based recall is real; WI-supat added collision precision on top (real self-analysis delta +94 calls edges once the finalize fix landed).\n\nWI-noham STAYS OPEN per its own closure-evidence discipline: the flagship deadness repros (Symbol.end_line, ValidationResult.ok) + the INV-nuzas 283-twin residual + the decorated/plain deadness deltas must be re-measured under a bakeoff / dead-code-maybe --seeds all before marking satisfied. All engineering is done; the remaining gate is that quantitative re-measure (awaits_bakeoff_validation)."  # ba6c
